# TLS front door for OpenWebUI — see docs/adr/0006-tls-reverse-proxy.md.
#
# `tls internal` makes Caddy mint and manage its own local CA + leaf certs
# (persisted in the caddy_data volume across restarts) instead of requesting
# one from a public CA — no domain name or internet-reachable port 80/443
# required, which fits a LAN/dev deployment. Browsers will show a one-time
# untrusted-certificate warning until that CA is trusted, or you replace this
# block with a real certificate — see the ADR for both.
#
# `on_demand` is required, not cosmetic: this site block has no static
# hostname (it's reached by whatever IP or name the client used — localhost
# via a tunnel, a LAN IP, a real hostname), and without `on_demand` Caddy
# never actually issues a certificate for an address it wasn't told about
# upfront — every handshake fails with a generic "internal error" TLS alert.
# `on_demand` mints one on the fly for whatever SNI shows up, safe here
# because the internal CA has no external rate limit to exhaust. Verified
# against both an IP-literal and a hostname client (see the ADR).
:8443 {
	tls internal {
		on_demand
	}

	reverse_proxy openwebui:8080
}
